 ## Threads and ownership
 
+`NshSurface.documentEditorDiagnostics(): DocumentEditorDiagnostic[]` reads the
+surface's current large-document Input owners on demand. It returns complete
+owned-source SHA256 and byte/UTF-16 lengths, target/generation/edit count,
+directional selection and active caret, viewport anchor/content dimensions,
+composition/focus/attachment state, requested/applied plan revisions, and owner-
+lifetime `documentDraws`/`caretDraws` callback counts. These counters advance only
+at the actual parent/caret draw entry points; reading them does not request a
+frame. The generated SDK declarations define the concrete record; an unapplied
+plan is null.
+It returns no document text. Hashing/export occurs only when explicitly called,
+not on a timer, edit or ordinary frame. It has no process-global input registry:
+only live slots belonging to this surface are inspected. A live surface without
+an active runtime/document returns an empty array; disposal, reentrant access,
+invalid diagnostic data and native-owner failures reject rather than pretending
+to be an empty result. This diagnostic API does not establish rendered/presented
+frames, native IME correctness or production large-document performance.
+
 One `Services` session spans NativeAbility Create/Destroy. N-API entry points
